---
// Case studies: whole problem spaces, described without answers, for the
// practice to work on. Door pages carry integer orders; their sub-pages x.1, x.2.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import RfcHint from '../../components/RfcHint.astro';
import { guide } from '../../lib/guide.mjs';
const g = guide();
const cases = g.pages.filter((p) => p.kind === 'case');
const doors = cases.filter((p) => Number.isInteger(p.order));
const subsOf = (d) => cases.filter((p) => !Number.isInteger(p.order) && Math.floor(p.order) === d.order);
const subTitle = (t) => { const x = t.replace(/^[^:]+:\s*/, ''); return x.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + x.slice(1); };
---
<Base title="Case studies" description="Whole capacity-planning problem spaces, described without answers, for the practice to work on." nav="cases">
  <div class="wrap wrap--reading">
    <div class="page-head">
      <p class="draft-tag">Guide · draft for review</p>
      <h1>Case studies</h1>
      <p class="in-short guide-short"><em>Whole problem spaces, described without answers, for the practice to work on.</em></p>
    </div>
    <RfcHint />
    <article class="prose reading-wrap">
      <p>A framework is easier to judge against a real-shaped problem. Each case here describes one capacity-planning problem space and leaves the answers open. The rules for writing one, and the case format, are on the guide's <a href="/guide/cases/">Cases page</a>.</p>
      <h2>Case 1: the launch that needed memory</h2>
      <p>The seed paper's worked example, told as a case: a launch approved on CPU alone, a memory question asked after its commit point, and a bill 30% over plan. <a href="/guide/cases/#case-1-the-launch-that-needed-memory">Read it on the Cases page</a>.</p>
      {doors.map((d) => (
        <>
          <h2>{d.title}</h2>
          <p>{d.short}</p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href={d.url}>The case page</a>: the situation in two minutes.</li>
            {subsOf(d).map((s) => <li><a href={s.url}>{subTitle(s.title)}</a>: {s.short}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </>
      ))}
      <h2>Add a case</h2>
      <p>Cases from your own experience follow the anonymization checklist; problem-space cases follow the four rules. Both are on the <a href="/guide/cases/">Cases page</a>, and every case starts as a <a href="https://github.com/anacay/cpp/discussions">discussion</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
